// Refined-lattice (fjc>1) MOMENT regression (ref 20 Aug 2026): the four
// excess-profile moment columns (1st_M_phi_z, 2nd_M_phi_z, RMS,
// fluctuations) on a planar FJC_choices 5 (fjc = 2) adsorption layer.
// Guards the 20 Aug 2026 fix of a double division by fjc in
// Lattice1D.moment (collaborator bug report): z_phys is in bond units and
// L is the physical layer volume (1/fjc), so the L-weighted sum is
// already the physical moment -- the extra /fjc copied from Namics'
// LGrad1::Moment in the 5 Jul 2026 physics review made every fjc>1
// moment fjc times too small (the review matched the inner /fjc but
// missed that Namics' 1st_M caller multiplies fjc back,
// segment.cpp:1837). SELF-VALIDATING at creation: kal 1st/2nd moments ==
// the physical integrals sum(z^n (phi-phib) dz)/theta_exc from the
// committed .pro at machine precision, and are fjc-CONSISTENT (fjc 1/2/3/4
// give <z> 1.494/1.309/1.272/1.258, converging under refinement, where the
// bug gave exactly <z>/fjc). NOT oracle-validated on PURPOSE: the compiled
// Namics' planar fjc>1 moments are garbage (its Moment loop sums the
// zeroed ghost rows, whose planar L = 1/fjc != 0 -- measured 1st_M -4.81
// where the physical value is +1.31), and its 2nd_M misses the *fjc
// compensation everywhere (both reported to the Namics authors). The
// curved branch of the SAME
// moment() line IS oracle-validated (spherical fjc = 2 colloid
// adsorption, ghost-clean in Namics): 1st_M matches the binary to 7e-7
// and 2nd_M comes out exactly fjc x Namics', pinning the missing *fjc.
// fjc = 1 moments are bit-identical to before the fix (factor 1); the
// fjc = 1 columns are guarded by brush_in_good_solvent.in and friends.
lat : NN : n_layers : 40
lat : NN : geometry : planar
lat : NN : lattice_type : hexagonal
lat : NN : FJC_choices : 5
lat : NN : lowerbound : surface

mon : S : freedom : frozen
mon : S : frozen_range : lowerbound
mon : A : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_S : -1.5
mon : A : chi_W : 0.4
mon : W : freedom : free

mol : pol : composition : (A)25
mol : pol : freedom : free
mol : pol : phibulk : 0.02

mol : W : composition : (W)1
mol : W : freedom : solvent

newton : NN : tolerance : 1e-8

output : kal : append : false
kal : mon : A : theta_exc
kal : mon : A : 1st_M_phi_z
kal : mon : A : 2nd_M_phi_z
kal : mon : A : RMS
kal : mon : A : fluctuations

output : pro : append : false
pro : mon : A : phi

start
